  "chapter": {
    "number": 75,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(76) For the end, among the Hymns, a Psalm for Asaph; a Song for the Assyrian."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "God is known in Judea: his name is great in Israel.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "And his place has been in",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 138
          },
          {
            "text": "peace, and his dwelling-place in Sion.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "There he broke the power of the bows, the shield, and the sword, and the battle. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You do wonderfully shine forth from the everlasting mountains.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "All the simple ones in heart were troubled; all the men of wealth have slept their sleep, and have found nothing in their hands.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "At your rebuke, O God of Jacob, the riders on horses slumbered.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You are terrible; and who shall withstand you, because of your anger?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You did cause judgment to be heard from heaven; the earth feared, and was still,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "when God arose to judgment, to save all the meek in heart. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "For the inward thought of man shall give thanks to you: and the memorial of his inward thought shall keep a feast to you.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Vow, and pay your vows to the Lord our God; all that are round about him shall bring gifts, even to him that is terrible,",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and that takes away the spirits of princes; to him that is terrible among the kings of the earth.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
    "footnotes": [
      {
        "noteId": 138,
        "caller": "+",
        "text": "Or, Salem, see the Hebrew.",
        "reference": {
          "chapter": 75,
          "verse": 2
        }
      }
    ]
  },
